(Title) Tj
T*
(Regional Anesthesia Techniques for Cesarean Delivery: Comparative Efficacy and Postpartum) Tj
T*
(Mental Health Outcomes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Adequate postoperative analgesia following cesarean section is essential for maternal) Tj
T*
(recovery and may influence postpartum mental health. Two regional anesthesia approaches) Tj
T*
(are commonly used, yet comparative effectiveness for pain control and mental health) Tj
T*
(outcomes remains unclear. This randomized study will compare two distinct regional) Tj
T*
(anesthesia blocks in women undergoing cesarean delivery. Sixty postoperative women will be) Tj
T*
(randomized 1:1 to receive either an erector spinae plane block or a transversus abdominis) Tj
T*
(plane block following their surgical procedure. Pain severity will be assessed using) Tj
T*
(standardized visual analog scales at multiple timepoints postoperatively. Secondary) Tj
T*
(outcomes include requirement for rescue analgesics, patient satisfaction with pain) Tj
T*
(management, and postpartum depression screening using standardized questionnaires at 4-6) Tj
T*
(weeks postpartum. All participants will receive standard postoperative care protocols.) Tj
T*
(This comparative effectiveness study will provide data on whether the choice of regional) Tj
T*
(anesthesia technique influences both acute pain outcomes and postpartum mood.) Tj
ET
